  "essence": [
    "拓印墨色加白纸的黑白两族",
    "黑色剪影配阴刻白线",
    "古拙简化的侧面造型与分层排布",
    "石面颗粒小坑与细微裂纹"
  ],
  "recipe": {
    "positive": "Visual style (follow exactly): stone-relief rubbing technique inspired by Han-dynasty carved stone slabs: black ink pad-dabbed on off-white paper, the scene rendered as flat low-relief silhouettes with incised white lines on a black ground, profile-view figures and objects with archaic simplified proportions, an arrangement in horizontal bands or registers when the scene allows, incised parallel lines for cloth and texture, simple cloud-scroll or geometric filler between forms, speckled ink with small stone-grain pits and a few tiny cracks. The whole scene is expressed as a rubbing at full bleed. Figures, faces, hair, clothing and objects come only from the current brief, including modern clothing and short hair, drawn as profile silhouettes without period costume.",
    "hard_constraints": [
      "Tone comes from ink density and stipple only, with no colour and no cast shadow.",
      "The picture shows the rubbed surface itself, never a photographed slab, stone frame or stele border."
    ],
    "text_mode": [
      "none"
    ]
  },
